#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# curl

#% text
# `curl(v, [x, y, z])` gives the curl of the three-dimensional vector field `v`.

#% text
# `curl([v1, v2], [x, y])` gives the scalar curl `d(v2, x) - d(v1, y)` of a plane field.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The variables are Cartesian coordinates.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
curl([-y, x, 0], [x, y, z])
#% output
#= [0, 0, 2]

#% cell
curl([x*y, y*z, z*x], [x, y, z])
#% output
#= [-y, -z, -x]

#% cell
curl([-y, x], [x, y])
#% output
#= 2

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# A gradient field has no curl (`expand` collects the terms):

#% cell
expand(curl(grad(sin(x*y) + z^2, [x, y, z]), [x, y, z]))
#% output
#= [0, 0, 0]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `grad`, `div`, `cross`
